{"name":"Legendary Sword","hex":"#7f8384","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"legendary","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to a legend or to legends.","Appearing (solely) in legends."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A collection of legends, in particular of lives of saints.","One who relates legends."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legendary"},{"term":"sword","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long bladed weapon with a grip and typically a pommel and crossguard (together forming a hilt), which is designed to cut, stab, slash and/or hack.","A suit in certain playing card decks, particularly those used in Spain and Italy, or those used for divination.\nA card of this suit."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stab or cut with a sword"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sword"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of mythological objects","blocks":[{"text":"Mythological objects encompass a variety of items found in mythology, legend, folklore, tall tale, fable, religion, spirituality, superstition, and the paranormal from across the world. This list is organized according to the category of object."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Joseph_Alanen_-_The_Forging_of_the_Sampo.jpg/330px-Joseph_Alanen_-_The_Forging_of_the_Sampo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_mythological_objects","wikidata":"Q3243129"},{"title":"Sword","blocks":[{"text":"A sword is an edged, bladed weapon intended for manual cutting or thrusting. Its blade, longer than that of a knife or dagger, is attached to a hilt and can be straight or curved. A thrusting sword tends to have a straighter blade with a pointed tip. A slashing sword is more likely to be curved and to have a sharpened cutting edge on one or both sides of the blade. Many swords are designed for both thrusting and slashing. The precise definition of a sword varies by historical epoch and geographic region."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sword","wikidata":"Q12791"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Achilles_fighting_against_Memnon_Leiden_Rijksmuseum_voor_Oudheden.jpg/500px-Achilles_fighting_against_Memnon_Leiden_Rijksmuseum_voor_Oudheden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Achilles_fighting_against_Memnon_Leiden_Rijksmuseum_voor_Oudheden.jpg/500px-Achilles_fighting_against_Memnon_Leiden_Rijksmuseum_voor_Oudheden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Achilles wearing his armor","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAchilles_fighting_against_Memnon_Leiden_Rijksmuseum_voor_Oudheden.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Shield_of_Achilles_%28illustration%29.jpg/500px-Shield_of_Achilles_%28illustration%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Shield_of_Achilles_%28illustration%29.jpg/500px-Shield_of_Achilles_%28illustration%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shield of Achilles (illustration)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShield_of_Achilles_(illustration).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Corona_immortalitatis.jpg/500px-Corona_immortalitatis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Corona_immortalitatis.jpg/500px-Corona_immortalitatis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Crown of Immortality, held by the allegorical figure Eterna (Eternity)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACorona_immortalita